{"en":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt5\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> One of three kinds of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/quasiparticle\" title=\"quasiparticle\">quasiparticle</a> (the others being the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/spinon\" title=\"spinon\">spinon</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/orbiton\" title=\"orbiton\">orbiton</a>) that <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/electron\" title=\"electron\">electrons</a> in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/solid\" title=\"solid\">solids</a> are able to split into during the process of spin–charge separation, when extremely tightly confined at temperatures close to absolute zero."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt20\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Something that is both a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/part\" title=\"part\">part</a> and a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/whole\" title=\"whole\">whole</a>."}]}],"got":[{"partOfSpeech":"Romanization","language":"Gothic","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt34\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">romanization of <span class=\"form-of-definition-link\"><i class=\"Goth mention\" lang=\"got\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/𐌷𐍉𐌻𐍉𐌽#Gothic\" title=\"𐌷𐍉𐌻𐍉𐌽\">𐌷𐍉𐌻𐍉𐌽</a></i></span></span>"}]}]}
